    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0652" n="612" xml:id="pg612"/>

                <head>267. Memorandum From the Director of the National Security Council Secretariat
                        (Boggs) to the National Security Council Planning Board<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d267-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1957</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Review of Long-Range U.S. Policy Toward the Near East</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>A. Record of Meeting of Planning Board, September 6, 1957, item 4<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d267-f2"/></item>
                    <item>B. Memo for Planning Board, September 5, 1957,<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d267-f3"/> and Memo for Board Assistants, September 16, 1957
                            (State)<anchor n="4" xml:id="d267-f4"/></item>
                    <item>C. Memo for Board Assistants, October 4, 1957 (Defense)<anchor n="5"
                            xml:id="d267-f5"/></item>
                    <item>D. Memo for Board Assistants, September 13, 1957 (CIA)<anchor n="6" xml:id="d267-f6"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed draft list of questions on the subject is transmitted herewith for
                    use by the Board Assistants at an early meeting in preparing a list of questions
                    for Planning Board discussion pursuant to Reference A.</p>
                <p>The enclosure consists of a topical arrangement, prepared by the NSC Staff, of the State, Defense and CIA questions circulated by References B–D,
                    supplemented by NSC Staff questions not
                    previously circulated. All questions submitted by State, Defense and CIA have been included in the enclosure with the
                    exception of No. 6 in the State list of September 5.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Marion W.
                                Boggs</hi><anchor n="7" xml:id="d267-f7"
                    /></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d267-a1.xml" xpointer="d267-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
