                <p>Not printed. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi>
                    S/P–NSC Files:
                    Lot 62 D 1)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f3" n="3" xml:id="d267-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d260">Document 260</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f4" n="4" xml:id="d267-f4-content">
                <p>Boggs’ memorandum of September 16
                    transmitted to the National Security Council Board Assistants the text of a
                    paper, prepared by the Department of State, that listed “Additional Questions
                    for Consideration in Review of United States Policy Toward the Near East (NSC 5428).” (Department of State, S/P–NSC Files: Lot
                    61 D 167, NSC 5801 File)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f5" n="5" xml:id="d267-f5-content">
                <p>Boggs’ memorandum of October 4 to the
                    National Security Council Board Assistants transmitted the text of a paper,
                    prepared by the Department of Defense, that listed “Possible Questions in
                    Connection With Review of Long-Range U.S. Policy in the Near East.” (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f6" n="6" xml:id="d267-f6-content">
                <p>Boggs’ memorandum of September 13
                    transmitted to the National Security Council Board Assistants the text of a
                    paper, prepared by the Central Intelligence Agency, entitled “CIA Comments and Questions.” (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f7" n="7" xml:id="d267-f7-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
